From: cut-card-proof-held
Subject: [PATCH] Hold the cut card's delivery proof for the tick, and stamp the terminal settle's audit entry

A cut card's proof is an un-awaited promise created at the pass's tail, and an
un-awaited promise is CANCELLED the instant the handler returns -- so the audit
entry never lands, no proof ever exists for the next check to refuse the repeat
on, and `dup-skip` is structurally unreachable. Live 2026-09-23: 12 `p:` marks,
zero with a proof in the ring.

Route both background proof writes through the tick's existing waitUntil
hand-off (worker.tickWaitUntil, already used for the deferred token_stats
writes with the same measured 100%-loss signature), and stamp the terminal
card's late settle with its own sig so its entry lands on the per-card key
instead of the coarse token key.

